{"t": 1794118450.2463133, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return page ``number`` (1-based) of ``items``, ``size`` items per page.\"\"\"\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "Fix 1-based pagination in page() (#57)", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794118453.6890905, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated the page number as 0-based, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page even though the API documents `?page=1` as the first page.\n\n## Fix\n\nCompute the slice offset from a 1-based page number:\n\n```python\nstart = (number - 1) * size\n```\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified locally with a 25-item list: page 1 -> items 1-10, page 2 -> items 11-20, page 3 -> items 21-25.\n\nFixes #57", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination in page()"}, "ok": true}
